KNOWNBUG
repeat1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.x == 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A repeat statement with an elaboration-time-constant count inside an always
block (IEEE 1800-2017 12.7.2). The type checker accepts it
(verilog_typecheckt::convert_repeat), but verilog_rtl_buildert::build_statement
in src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp has no case for ID_repeat and aborts with
"statement `repeat' is not supported by RTL construction" (CONVERSION ERROR).
A constant-count repeat loop should be unrolled during RTL construction the
same way build_for unrolls for loops; the former verilog_synthesis module did
this in synth_repeat (removed in commit a445c7fd). The loop body runs exactly
three times, so x must equal 3.
